## Reversible compilation rule

A Boolean SSA block has explicit immutable input wires and fresh zero targets
for AND, XOR, NOT, COPY and literal nodes. AND has one Toffoli; XOR has two
CNOTs; NOT has one X and one CNOT; COPY has one CNOT; a one literal has one X.
Repeated operands are simplified before emitting any gate with aliased
controls. Wire metadata and generator execution are not confused with actual
data movement: static rewiring is free circuit wiring, while data-dependent
selection is compiled to gates over every possible entry.

Let `(a,x,n,c,u)` count these nodes, where `u` counts one literals, and let
`g = 5a + 2x + 2n + c + u`. Let `o` be output bits, with duplicates allowed.
Compute all nodes, CNOT the designated outputs into disjoint arbitrary output
targets, then reverse every node. This implements

```
|input, z, 0_history, 0_kernel_work>
 -> |input, z XOR f(input), 0_history, 0_kernel_work>.
```

It costs `2g+o` elementary gates plus the separately doubled counts for
declared clean response-XOR kernels/oracles. History has one fresh bit per
Boolean node and each kernel output bit, plus the maximum simultaneously used
clean kernel workspace. Inputs, random tape and caller output targets are
additional. These exact formulas describe an actual emitted circuit, not a
conversion of mixed AES/loop counts into elementary gates.

For compositional loops, every iteration's fresh node/output wires are kept
until reverse traversal. Thus history grows with the full unrolled count;
reusing a scratch register is permitted only for a kernel that proves it
returns that register to zero. Fixed loop bounds and the offset mapping of
random-tape segments are public circuit structure. Resource summaries are
derived from checked block structure and repeat counts, never accepted as
caller assertions about unknown code.

A fixed response-XOR oracle can be called again to uncompute its result.
An external *classical* PRP challenge interface is not such an inverse oracle:
an entry reduction must retain that interaction's transcript and separately
price it. This machine does not silently promote the proposed PRP interface
to coherent access. Public AES and concrete Keccak implementations also need
their own executable circuits or explicit unresolved resource parameters.

## Schedule semantics and projection

For a public cap M, fixed input tapes contain M primary and M auxiliary
256-bit values. Compute all predicates and the first accepted position with
fixed loops. The actual source's early stopping is recovered by an active
prefix flag: primary writes use exactly that prefix, auxiliary values never
produce writes, and no auxiliary selection is enabled after primary success.
The selected challenge starts at zero, so two exhausted scans yield the frozen
zero fallback. An unused random-tape suffix is independent private material
and has no public effect; presampling it changes no output/log distribution.
Nevertheless its full random preparation and wire inventory are charged.

The primary zero-based trial counter is a separate 32-bit value from both the
attempt count and the log append counter. The count of attempted primary or
auxiliary draws may equal M and needs `ceil(log2(M+1))` bits. Exhaustion returns
an error, never a proof carrying a fabricated counter. Canonical zero values
in fields unused by that error branch are internal conventions only.

`Schedule.emit_clean` is a lazy emitter for every admitted cap through 2^20.
It computes each iteration's input/output wire labels from public offsets;
it does not store a million frame descriptions or random-tape wire lists.
Only `wiring()`, the optional materialized finite-test view, restricts its cap
to 32. The production gate counts refer to the same lazy emitter. Both
templates produce fresh state-output wires, an invariant checked before using
the closed-form repeat mapping. A full clean scheduler uses 4M invocations of
the clean admissibility kernel: 2M while computing and 2M during reversal.

Presampling is an exact private-state extension, not equality of consumed RNG
byte offsets. For every fixed selected row and entering external state, the
first admissible prefix of the primary tape has the original stopping-time
law. Its unused suffix is independent conditional on that prefix. If primary
exhausts, the independent auxiliary tape has the same bounded stopping/fallback
law. If it succeeds, no auxiliary bit influences the outputs. Coins for later
fields use separate independent slots. Averaging over and tracing the unused
private coins therefore preserves the joint external state, not only a
standalone proof distribution: no scheduler instruction reads or modifies the
base oracle or adversary registers. This local fact still needs composition
with W0's prefix-enabled writes; it is not a claim that W0 is implemented.

## Direct opening phase

`opening.py` takes the selected admissible challenge, 112*tau fresh commitment
bytes and T_open fixed 32-byte key slots. It computes all heap marks and the
frontier count r using the pinned predicate helper's compute/inverse routines.
It copies the marks, count, and child-XOR flags in descending parent order,
then reverses that geometry computation. The predicate-only target is never
used. Thus each geometry call returns its scratch to zero. This is a new
explicit composition of reviewed routines, requiring its own local review.

For each public slot j, a Boolean comparator computes j<r. Each of that key
slot's 256 bits is ANDed with the comparator, so the opening is the sampled
commitments followed by the first r supplied keys and zero padding. Hidden
indices use their source low-bit-first slices with zero extension to 16 bits.
There is no secret memory address: comparators and key gates use static wire
indices. For each fixed admissible opening, projecting away the independent
unused key suffix gives exactly the frozen direct material sampler's coins.

Let n=L and d=ceil(log2 L). The clean geometry kernel computes and reverses
the source-shaped marks/count work once each, with

```
Toffoli = 2*sum_i 2^depth_i*(2*depth_i-3)
          + 2*(n-1)*(1+(d-1)^2),
CNOT = 14*(n-1) + (2*n-1) + d + 2*(n-1),
X = 2*sum_i 2^depth_i*depth_i.
```

The added CNOT terms copy marks, count and two child bits for each frontier
flag. Its clean-work allocation is the predicate's marks/count/flag/ladder
region; the unused predicate target is excluded. The complete opening block
then applies the same SSA clean-embedding rule, including all comparators,
key masks, opening bytes, decoded indices and intermediate geometry outputs.
Its current counts are 21,358,067 candidate and 308,370,886 comparator elementary
gates; these include this block's own compute/copy/uncompute, not surrounding
whole-machine composition. No base-oracle calls occur here.

These outputs are **internal stage registers**, not an additional adversarial
interface. In particular, the final exhausted request must not expose its
selected challenge, opening, geometry or count history. The separately implemented B1 stage routes the source-order keys into their
actual heap slots. B0-to-B1 wiring and the E0 projection exposing only the
defined proof or error are still required; constructing registers alone does
not establish either composition.

The finite tests cover the implemented stage boundaries. It exhaustively checks small schedule
acceptance patterns and comparisons, directly interprets emitted reversible
gates with arbitrary output targets, checks cleanup/inversion/counts, and
checks both real zero-fallback openings (11/12 keys and 11,024/9,664 bytes).
The full simulator, full resource vector and cryptographic entry remain open.

## B1 supplied-material reconstruction

`bavc_machine.py` scans every parent in descending order and selects the next
frontier key by comparing its secret rank with each fixed slot. Both zero and
duplicate key values are legal. `prg_machine.py` then scans every parent in
ascending order, reading its key from its earlier parent's fresh output.
It computes four AES blocks using source little-endian low32+counter and
high32+parent additions, with no carry across either word. A marked parent
retains its initial children. All otherwise-unused AES computations are charged
and uncomputed. The kernel is the separately reviewed **concrete public AES**
circuit; this extra work is not valid for an external classical PRP challenge.

`leaf_machine.py` follows source vector/index order and interleaved heap
positions. It computes all nine AES blocks, splits seed32/b0[96]/b1[16], and
uses the authenticated GF(2^768) and GF(2^256) kernels for the actual affine
commitment. Marked leaves select their cached hidden commitment and a zero
seed. Their dummy public computations are also charged and cleaned. Its H0
input must originate from the same invocation; the surrounding composition
supplies it, rather than treating it as free randomness.

`hash_machine.py` uses fixed-length restrictions of **one shared immutable**
byte-string response-XOR function F with a 264-byte response. Different
`F:length` opcodes do not denote independent functions. Preparing input bytes,
including the final domain byte, is explicit CNOT/X work. Producing a shorter
response prefix costs two full F calls, the prefix-copy CNOTs, and 2,112 clean
response bits. No concrete SHAKE permutation is included in these oracle calls.
H0/H1 addresses end in 0/1, so they cannot match the IdealPublic chronological
writes ending in 9/10/11. This exact disjointness permits the base interface in
these two domains; it does not remove the overlay from external queries.

H0's clean map costs 2 F calls and 2,512 CNOT, with 2,864 clean work bits.
H1 stores the tau vector digests, constructs the outer digest in source order,
then reverses the vector computations. Its exact clean cost is
`F=4*tau+2`, `X=4*tau+2`, and `CNOT=3584*L+4512*tau+1744`.
It retains `512*tau` digest bits, 2,112 response bits and one maximum-sized
query frame; these are all returned to zero. Seed bytes never enter H1.

`reconstruction.py` joins the complete B1 algorithm at the supplied canonical
material boundary. Inputs are namespace77, IV16, source hidden marks, canonical
frontier key slots and the tau cached hidden commitments. It retains the routed
heap, expanded heap, H0 result and ordered seed/commitment records, but shares
the maximum clean workspace of the component circuits. It computes routing,
tree expansion, H0 and leaf records; H1 writes the final commitment output;
seeds are copied; leaf/H0/tree/routing are reversed in that order. Its output is
`commitment64 || vector-ordered seeds32*L`, XORed into an arbitrary disjoint
target. All intermediate state returns to zero. The clean cost is exactly
`2*(R+T+H0+Leaf)+H1+256*L CNOT`, with `4*tau+6` full base queries.

This identity is conditional on the canonical admissible input relation, the
concrete kernel contracts, one immutable base function, and atomic requests.
It follows as a joint permutation on source/output/base/adversary registers;
source basis labels are preserved while their reduced state may become
entangled with the output. The reverse calls use the unchanged function and
source registers. No intervening log mutation or adversary query is hidden
inside the clean embedding. B0-to-B1 wiring, later VOLE/relation work, persistent
log history and final public projection are still open full-machine stages.

## V0/V1 supplied-material composition

The derivation and exact component formulas are in `V0-design.md`. V0 scans
all original seed slots, reconstructs the source hidden-index column fold with
controlled XORs, applies c_1 through c_(tau-1) only to the first ell bits, and
uses the actual tree moduli for the ten low-mask shares. Every row expansion
is the charged concrete AES circuit, including unused hidden-seed work. No
secret input controls an unpriced memory address.

V1 uses the literal pinned G, W_CRT, W_TREE and W_GATE bits. It emits every
selected linear CNOT, creates each actual 162-byte H5 address, reads the low
ten bits via the shared full-response F, applies the gamma-selected correction,
adds the gate contribution, then clears the correction and hash response.
The source mask order0..9 is retained: indices0..5 feed QuickSilver and the
VOLE folded head; indices6..9 are the four additive VOLE final masks.

`vole_reconstruction.py` computes V0 into retained zero columns/shares, runs
V1 into the arbitrary caller Delta||Q||q_masks XOR targets, then repeats V0 to
clear the retained columns/shares. Its exact cost is `2*V0+V1`; work is the
retained V0 output plus the maximum component workspace. The unchanged F and
input labels guarantee the clean reverse. H5 final byte5 is disjoint from
programmed writes9/10/11. Full request wiring must establish that the hidden
u16 indices decode the same selector, that its grinding tail is zero, and
that all supplied seed/correction/namespace/IV material belongs to this request.
The component does not itself validate these cross-stage input relations.

Finite tests cover full small-shape joint maps, arbitrary targets, cleanup,
source fold references, both actual table orientations and every selected
residue basis image. Actual-row emitter resource traversal is a static circuit
count, not execution of the huge production circuit. The report lists the
V0/V1 composition separately for each role and retains every full-coverage,
primitive-entry and qualification flag as false.

## What a completed machine would and would not establish

Complete IR coverage could give a conservative, finite, source-bound resource
vector for this mathematical simulator relative to its named base oracle.
It would not establish that a concrete SHAKE oracle is an independent QROM,
that the actual-input AES hybrids embed in an accepted premise, that this
simulator replaces the frozen real-root Sim+ in its application premise, or
that any primitive retains security at the resulting driver resources.

The frozen linear-scan overlay alone has an illustrative elementary upper
bound around 2^153.761 at T=2^44 and Q_ext=2^64. Completing a possibly still
larger conservative bound can close an unknown-resource item without making
that bound useful for a 2^128 attack assessment. It is an upper bound for one
construction, not a lower bound or a proof of insecurity. Efficient structures
would need their own coherent implementation, without assuming quantum RAM.

The complete adversary, advice/preprocessing, chosen-input entry drivers,
earlier game transitions and final comparisons remain separate obligations.
Independent cryptographic review, owner acceptance and exact required hardware
qualification remain external to local circuit/source proofs. This proposal
does not claim physical 64 MiB verifier workspace or any runtime measurement.

Primary context: Bennett's reversible simulation is a construction after a
machine and its time/space bounds are supplied; its asymptotic theorem is not
a concrete compiler-cost certificate for this Rust source. See
https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/0218053 . The explicit SSA rule above states
its own gate accounting and will be checked on finite circuits.
